# POISONED FIXTURE unit 3 of 6 — expected outcome: CRASHED (status 137, SIGKILL/OOM)
#
# HONESTY NOTE — same caveat as unit 2, and one extra reason here.
#
# A genuine compile-time OOM is not reproducible on this host: it is at
# ~103/125 GB with 100+ `simple` processes, and `earlyoom` is configured to
# prefer killing `simple`. Deliberately exhausting memory would therefore (a)
# take the whole box down and (b) most likely arrive as SIGTERM from earlyoom
# (143 = TERMINATED = UNVERIFIED), not the SIGKILL(137) this unit is meant to
# exercise. So the harness induces it deterministically as
# `sh -c 'kill -KILL $$'`.
#
#   DOES prove — a REAL wait status of 137 from a REAL SIGKILL is classified
#     CRASHED (a signal death of the compiler is the compiler's problem), and is
#     kept DISJOINT from the 143/SIGTERM case, which must stay UNVERIFIED.
#   Does NOT prove — that this source exhausts memory. It does not.

fn oom_unit_three(n: i64) -> i64:
    n * 3
